Naming and the non-removable layers
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Apache License grants broad rights to use, modify, and redistribute this work,
including commercially. It does NOT grant rights to the project's names or marks
(Apache-2.0 Section 6, "Trademarks").

FPCOS defines four layers that a conformant inheriting skill may not remove:

    L0  Reality Anchor
    L1  Axiom Gate
    L4  Shadow Gate  (non-skippable self-critique)
    L5  Synthesis

A derivative that removes any of L0, L1, L4, or L5 MUST NOT be presented as
"First Principle Codex OS" or "FPCOS", and MUST NOT imply endorsement by the
author. Those layers are what the OS is; a version without them is a different
thing wearing the name.

This is a naming and accuracy requirement, not a restriction on use. The software
freedoms granted by the Apache License are not conditioned on it.

